    "long_instructions": "## Explore Product Filters\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Click **Tops**. Watch how the product grid changes.\r\n\r\n2. In **script.js**, highlight the `filterTops()` function and ask AI:\r\n\r\n   > How does the `filterTops()` function use `.map()`, an `if` statement, and `.push()` to decide which products stay in the list?\r\n\r\n3. Check the AI’s response:\r\n\r\n   * Does the explanation match what you observed after clicking **Tops**?\r\n   * What condition does the code check?\r\n   * Which product property is being used to make the decision?\r\n\r\n4. Above `filterTops()`, add a `//` comment explaining which products it keeps.\r\n\r\n5. Repeat these steps for the other filter buttons and functions:\r\n\r\n   * **Under $50** → `filterUnder50()`\r\n   * **Selling Fast** → `filterSellingFast()`\r\n   * **All** → `showAllProducts()`\r\n",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Teacher Notes: Explore Product Filters\r\n\r\nIn this level, students explore how the H&HEM app uses filter buttons to change which products appear on the page.\r\n\r\nThe goal is for students to understand that the **button itself is not the filter**. The button only triggers a function. The actual filter is the **condition inside the function** that decides whether each product should be kept or left out.\r\n\r\nStudents are expected to:\r\n\r\n* click each filter button and observe how the product grid changes\r\n* connect the button behavior to the matching function in `script.js`\r\n* identify the condition used inside each filter function\r\n* use the code as evidence to check whether the AI’s explanation is accurate\r\n* add comments that explain what each filter function keeps\r\n\r\nThis level reinforces a key programming idea:\r\n\r\n**A filter checks each item in a list and keeps only the items that match a condition.**\r\n\r\nThe code pattern students should notice is:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nproductsArray.map((product) => {\r\n  if (product.category === \"Tops\") {\r\n    displayProductsArray.push(product);\r\n  }\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nStudents do not need to master every detail of objects yet. They should focus on the relationship between:\r\n\r\n* the product data in `data.js`\r\n* the condition in the `if` statement\r\n* the products that appear after the page re-renders\r\n\r\n"
  },
